        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: باک",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "باک (bâk) — \"a fuel tank (of a car)\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "باک (bâk) ماشین تقریبا خالی است. Bâk-e mâshin taqriban khâli ast. The car's tank is almost empty."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Bâk râ por kardan — to fill the tank. A different, older bâk means fear."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "bâk 'fuel tank' was borrowed from Russian and is usually traced to Russian bak 'a tank'. EtymDB lists Russian bak only with a different, nautical sense, so the line is hedged."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
